; bfsodium KDF_FB_SHA_256 : NIST SP 800_108r1 section 4 2  feedback mode
;
; HAND WRITTEN skeleton; The pseudorandom function is sha256/hmac  PASTED  and
; entered once per thirty two bytes of output; The counter is stepped by
; chacha20/add32  PASTED;
;
; As in sha256/hashcore  a run of ONE repeated token is a repetition rather
; than a decision and is written as such; every offset and every branch below
; was worked out from the map and written down;
;
; IO  in:  klen{2} LE  fixedlen{2} LE  okmlen{2} LE  kbuf{256}  fixedbuf{256}
;          iv{32}
;     out: okm{okmlen}
;
; Only the first klen bytes of the key buffer are looked at  and the same for
; the fixed input; the rest MUST be nought; the whole of the IV is looked at;
;
; Feedback mode differs from counter mode in one thing: the block just made is
; the head of the next message; So
;   K{0} is the IV  and  K{i} is PRF( key  K{i minus 1} then i then fixed )
; which is the standard's own arrangement in section 4 2;
;
; ALL THREE PARTS OF THE MESSAGE HAVE FIXED LENGTHS  a block of thirty two  a
; counter of four and the fixed input after them  so all three land at cells
; this map names and NOTHING IS PLACED BY SLIDING; that is the whole reason
; this file is as short as its counter mode sibling;
;
; THE IV IS ALWAYS PRESENT AND ALWAYS THIRTY TWO BYTES; the standard allows an
; empty one  and an empty one would make the FIRST turn structurally different
; from every later turn  with the fixed input at offset four rather than
; thirty six; That is the special case the arrangement above exists to avoid
; so it is declined and said so  rather than paid for;
;
; FIXEDLEN IS AT MOST A HUNDRED AND FIFTY SIX  which is a hundred and ninety
; two less the block and the counter; a hundred and ninety two is the most
; sha256/hmac takes from memory  because sha256/hashcore's prefix buffer is
; two hundred and fifty six and the key pad block takes a quarter of it;
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x000:0x001  klen{2}      u16 LE  the key's length
;   @0x002:0x003  fixedlen{2}  u16 LE  the fixed input's length
;   @0x004:0x005  okmlen{2}    u16 LE  how many bytes are wanted
;   @0x006:0x105  kbuf{256}    u8      the key  as given
;   @0x106:0x205  fixedbuf{256} u8     the fixed input  as given
;   @0x206:0x225  K{32}        u8      K{i minus 1}; THE IV IS READ STRAIGHT
;                          INTO IT  so the first turn needs no special case
;   @0x228:0x327  ktemp{256}   u8      hands the key back after a copy
;   @0x328:0x427  ftemp{256}   u8      hands the fixed input back after a copy
;   @0x428:0x43a  the adder frame; chacha20/add32 footprint 0:19 at @0x428
;                 its a{4} IS THE COUNTER  little endian
;   @0x43c:0x43f  ctmp{4}      hands the counter back after a copy
;   @0x440:0x447  owedlo owedhi chances flag test back and two spare cells
;   @0x448:0x467  Kout{32}     the copy that is written out and spent
;   @0x470:0xb7b  sha256/hmac's frame  pasted at @0x470; footprint 0:1803
;
; K IS NOT HANDED BACK AFTER ITS COPY  and the key and the fixed input are;
; the difference is that K is SPENT by design: the mac that replaces it is
; written into K and into Kout at once  by one token with two destinations;
;
; THE COUNT STILL OWED IS KEPT WHERE IT IS TESTED; okmlen arrives at @0x004
; and moves into the counts frame before the first turn  because the test runs
; once per byte written out;
;
; Nothing buffers the output; each K is written as it is made and the last is
; cut short  so the tape does not grow with the length asked for;
;
; A digest is a byte string and hmac leaves its answer as eight little endian
; words  so the copy out reverses each word;

; read the three lengths  the two buffers and the IV
,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,
